### Describe the bug

After upgrading from 4.0.6 to 4.0.7, some `instanceof` checks started returning false when using `jsdom`.

```ts
console.log(request instanceof Request); // true
console.log(request.clone() instanceof Request); // false?
```

This seems related to the custom request class introduced in https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commit/a1b7361ab171e03daf4900141fd7502b1ccc1844.

Rolling back to 4.0.6 solves the issue, as well as changing the environment to `node`.

### Reproduction

https://github.com/diego-aquino/vitest-jsdom-request-clone-instanceof

1. `pnpm install`
2. `pnpm test`

I've added [some test cases](https://github.com/diego-aquino/vitest-jsdom-request-clone-instanceof/blob/main/example.test.ts) reproducing the `instanceof` problems. The tests pass on version 4.0.6 and fail starting with version 4.0.7.

```ts
it('requests should be instances of the global Request class', async () => {
  const request = new Request('http://localhost:3000/example');

  expect(request instanceof Request).toBe(true);
  expect(request).toBeInstanceOf(Request);

  expect(request instanceof global.Request).toBe(true);
  expect(request).toBeInstanceOf(global.Request);

  expect(request instanceof globalThis.Request).toBe(true);
  expect(request).toBeInstanceOf(globalThis.Request);
});

it('cloned requests should be instances of the global Request class', async () => {
  const request = new Request('http://localhost:3000/example');
  const requestClone = request.clone();

  expect(requestClone instanceof Request).toBe(true);
  expect(requestClone).toBeInstanceOf(Request);

  expect(requestClone instanceof global.Request).toBe(true);
  expect(requestClone).toBeInstanceOf(global.Request);

  expect(requestClone instanceof globalThis.Request).toBe(true);
  expect(requestClone).toBeInstanceOf(globalThis.Request);
});
```

