> How to test `dist/index.cjs` without modifying the source code, but using the configuration of vitest?

Use alias: https://vitest.dev/config/alias.html

Or `resolve.conditions` if it's a package:

```ts
export default defineConfig({
  resolve: {
    conditions: ['cjs-condition'],
  },
  ssr: {
    resolve: {
      condition: ['cjs-condition'],
    },
  }
})
```

`cjs-condition` is the name in the [exports map](https://nodejs.org/api/packages.html#subpath-exports) (I don't know which one is correct for your package)

In terms of "object shape", `Map` and `Set` is equivalent to empty object `{}`. Then if empty object on the right, `toMatchObject({})` is essentially no-op, so that's what's happening:

