maintainer_reply:
Named exports and default exports are [different things](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Guide/Modules#default_exports_versus_named_exports). Your named exports example doesn't work because you are mocking a default export:

```ts
import os from 'node:os'; // <- this is a default import

vi.spyOn(os, 'loadavg').mockReturnValue([0.2, 0, 0]);
```

Instead, you need to spy the named export:

```ts
import * as os from 'node:os'; // <- this is a namespace import

vi.spyOn(os, 'loadavg').mockReturnValue([0.2, 0, 0]);
```

Or you can do both at the same time:

```ts
import * as os from 'node:os';

vi.spyOn(os, 'loadavg').mockReturnValue([0.2, 0, 0]);
vi.spyOn(os.default, 'loadavg').mockReturnValue([0.2, 0, 0]);
```

