maintainer_reply:
Based on the discussion on Discord earlier, basically what this issue is about is:

```ts
import { defineConfig } from "vitest/config";

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    projects: [
      {
        plugins: [{ name: 'plugin:one', config() { console.log("Config one") } }],
        test: { name: "one" },
      },
      {
        plugins: [{ name: 'plugin:two', config() { console.log("Config two") } }],
        test: { name: "two" },
      },
    ],
  },
});
```

```sh
$ vitest --project one

Config one
Config two
```

User does not expect `Config two` to be logged at all, since `--project one` filters it out.

The project filtering should happen before ~~config resolution~~ plugin initialization. Of course this would be impossible in cases like:

```ts
import { defineConfig } from "vitest/config";

export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    projects: [
      {
        plugins: [
          {
            name: "plugin:one",
            config() {
              console.log("Config one");
            },
          },
        ],
        test: { name: "one" },
      },
      {
        plugins: [{ name: "plugin:two", config() { return { test: { name: "two" } } } }],
      },
    ],
  },
});
```

I think we could expose a way to specify your own VSC "provider". In the builtin git one we only have a single public method:

```ts
class VCSProvider {
  findChangedFiles(options: { cwd: string, changedSince?: string | boolean }): Promise<string[] | null>
}
```

Similarly like we do with [the sequencer](https://vitest.dev/config/sequence.html#sequence-sequencer), for example:

```ts
export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    vcsProvider: CustomVCSProvider,
  },
})
```

Or better just an object with that field:

```ts
export default defineConfig({
  test: {
    vcsProvider: new CustomVCSProvider(),
  },
})
```

