Hi! 👋 

Firstly, thanks for your work on this project! 🙂

Today I used [patch-package](https://github.com/ds300/patch-package) to patch `@vitest/pretty-format@4.1.8` for the project I'm working on.

I'm using `@xmldom/xmldom@0.8.13` and it's `Node.attributes` is not iterable. This was fixed in version 0.9 (https://github.com/xmldom/xmldom/issues/633), but I'm stuck on 0.8 for now.

Here is the diff that solved my problem:

```diff
diff --git a/node_modules/@vitest/pretty-format/dist/index.js b/node_modules/@vitest/pretty-format/dist/index.js
index daae2b0..6f2f434 100644
--- a/node_modules/@vitest/pretty-format/dist/index.js
+++ b/node_modules/@vitest/pretty-format/dist/index.js
@@ -328,7 +328,7 @@ function serializeDOM(node, config, indentation, depth, refs, printer, filterNod
 	const shadowChildren = nodeIsFragment(node) || !node.shadowRoot ? [] : Array.prototype.slice.call(node.shadowRoot.children);
 	const resolvedChildren = filterNode ? filterChildren(children, filterNode) : children;
 	const resolvedShadowChildren = filterNode ? filterChildren(shadowChildren, filterNode) : shadowChildren;
